<para>The scatter plot below displays the data on body mass and bite force for the crocodilians in the study. </para>
<para><figure><media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS BODY MASS IN POUNDS ON THE X-AXIS AND BITE FORCE IN POUNDS ON THE Y-AXIS."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/317164bf68f6bdd79eba0b950a1c841f1927321e"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Using technology, the line of best fit for the data is \(y=3.02x +154.68\).</para>
<para>The slope of the line of best fit is 3.02. This signifies that for every pound more the crocodile weighs, it has 3.02 more pounds of bite force.</para>
<para>The \(y\)-intercept is 154.68, which doesn’t quite make sense for a crocodile that weighs 0 pounds but does give a minimum bite force to expect from a crocodile.</para>
<title>Try It: Technology for Best Fitting Lines</title>
